  "finding": "Current R2530@2 defines Path as one or more strings listing Scope Unit identities in the root-to-target chain. R2530@3 changes that to one slash-delimited string of exact Names with root /. The former Header.Container path reference motivated integration, but the original proposal manifest explicitly records a separate operator selection of the scalar Name-based Path; IDs-only Container addresses do not logically revoke that earlier Path decision.",
  "consumers": "R1661 and R2689 require paths/depth derived from declared ancestry and not authored or authoritative; R1688 specifies ordered project-relative scope path and R1730 preserves ancestry independent of Labels. None of these exact claims requires the @3 one-string encoding. R970 requires unique Names, not slash encoding. A1319/A1321 Draft proposals and Epic planning currently name the scalar path decision and need coordinated update if it is withdrawn.",
  "disposition": "Remove R2530@3 as a prerequisite of the Header.Container ID-only source batch. Preserve Current R2530@2; hold @3 rather than withdraw it automatically until the independently recorded scalar Path decision is confirmed or explicitly superseded. No new Path feature or native mutation.",
  "question": "Does the earlier chosen scalar Name-based Scope Unit.Path remain desired independently of Header.Container, or should its Draft be withdrawn and the Current identity-chain representation retained?",
  "limits": "No native sources, code, tests, Workflow, Workbench or Git mutation."
}
